    "done_when": "Two parts, in order. (1) imas_ambix/data/selene_deck.py build_pf_passive gives every pf_passive loop a name, VV1, VV2 and so on in deck order, as the same module names probes MP1, MP2 and so on and flux loops FL1, FL2 and so on. A test in tests/data/test_selene_deck.py converts the deck fixtures and asserts that every entry of every first-level struct array the converter writes (pf_active coil, pf_passive loop, magnetics b_field_pol_probe and flux_loop, tf coil, and any other) carries a non-empty name, unique within its array. This session runs inside the fleet SLURM allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID is set), so the gate runs in place: TMPDIR=/tmp UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 4 tests/data/test_selene_deck.py > <your log> 2>&1; echo EXIT=$?, exiting 0, with the gate log header naming the base revision and the delta against it. UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. Commit that change. (2) Then re-convert both phases with write_phase_description from this worktree's committed code, reading only the sha256-verified copies already in /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/source/ (EQSLE.DATA, geo.in, coil_vv_OP2.dat; refuse if any sha256 differs from /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/source/provenance.json). Before overwriting, record the sha256 of every existing file in /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/OP1/ and /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/OP2/; then write new pf_active.nc, pf_passive.nc, magnetics.nc, wall.nc, tf.nc and receipt.json into each, with each receipt naming this run's converter commit. Read every file back through imas.DBEntry at DD 4.1.1: OP1 pf_passive holds loops VV1 (63 elements) and VV2 (57), OP2 holds VV1 (98), and the 12 pf_active coils still hold 40, 40, 40, 40, 16, 16, 16, 16, 16, 16, 6 and 6 elements. The evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-passive-loop-names.html lists, per phase and file, the replaced sha256 beside the new one, the loop names and element counts read back, and the converter commit. Nothing outside /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/OP1 and /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/OP2 is written under /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description. This node never contacts the JT-60SA server (no ssh jt-60sa, no EDDB call).",
